---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../lib/articles.js';
---
<Base schema={[{ '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': 'https://wesandwoodward.com/about/', url: 'https://wesandwoodward.com/about/', name: 'About Wes & Woodward', isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://wesandwoodward.com/#website' }, mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://wesandwoodward.com/#org' } }, AUTHOR]} title="About — Wes & Woodward">
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">About Wes &amp; Woodward</h1>
      <p>
        My name is <span id="author">Mark Wesley</span> (the &ldquo;Wes&rdquo; in &ldquo;Wes &amp; Woodward&rdquo;).
        I&rsquo;ve been a fan of the Red Wings since I was born, and a fan of data since 2016.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website combines two of the things I love: writing and asking why. Maybe that
        order is wrong. I love asking why and then writing about it. Consider Wes &amp; Woodward
        a passion project for people like me who want to know the numbers behind what their
        eyes are telling them.
      </p>
      <p>
        My goal for this site is to provide an outlet for Red Wings fans who love to geek out
        about advanced analytics.
      </p>
      <p>
        &ldquo;Why don&rsquo;t you expand this to the rest of the NHL?&rdquo; you might ask. First, I
        don&rsquo;t care about the rest of the NHL. I care about the Red Wings, and I will not
        bandwagon for anyone. Second, if I do write about the rest of the NHL, it&rsquo;s through
        the lens that the Red Wings are the center of the universe and the other 31 teams
        revolve around them.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you like what I&rsquo;m doing, that&rsquo;s great! I don&rsquo;t have any ulterior motives,
        I&rsquo;m not trying to sell you anything, and I&rsquo;m not planning on turning this site
        into a money-making venture. I just want to answer the questions I&rsquo;m curious about
        and improve my writing skills.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
